cli-list-presets-about = Lists all presets from a connected Line 6 device.
cli-list-presets-long = Probes the USB bus automatically if no device is specified.
cli-preset-category-about = Manage, list, and modify device presets.
cli-setlist-category-about = List the device's setlists.
cli-list-setlists-about = Lists the setlists on a connected Line 6 device.
cli-list-setlists-long = Reads the setlist names stored on the device. HX Stomp-family devices report a single setlist.
cli-total-setlists = Total: { $count } setlist(s) read.
cli-device-help = Target a specific device instead of auto-detecting.
cli-connecting-to = Connecting to { $device_name } …
cli-probing-usb = No device specified — probing USB bus for any supported Line 6 device...
cli-connected-to = Connected to: { $profile }
cli-total-presets = Total: { $count } preset(s) read.
cli-setlist-help = Setlist index, 0-based. Only Helix-family devices hold more than one.
cli-reading-setlist = Reading setlist { $setlist }...
cli-select-preset-about = Selects a specific preset on the device
cli-select-preset-long = Switches the active preset on the connected Line 6 device by providing the setlist and preset indices.
cli-selecting-preset = Selecting setlist { $setlist }, preset { $preset }...
cli-preset-selected-success = Preset successfully selected!
cli-rename-preset-about = Renames a preset on the device
cli-rename-preset-long = Stores a new name for the preset at the given setlist and preset indices. Names hold up to 16 printable ASCII characters.
cli-name-help = New preset name (up to 16 printable ASCII characters).
cli-renaming-preset = Renaming setlist { $setlist }, preset { $preset } to "{ $name }"...
cli-preset-renamed-success = Preset successfully renamed!
cli-preset-blocks-about = Shows the blocks of the active preset
cli-preset-blocks-long = Reads the active preset from the device and lists its blocks in signal order, with their models and parameter values.
cli-total-blocks = Total: { $count } block(s).
cli-path-split = Path 2 runs parallel to positions { $from }–{ $to } of path 1.
cli-preset-active-about = Shows which preset is active on the device
cli-preset-active-long = Asks the device for its active preset and prints its setlist, slot and name.
cli-active-preset = Active preset: setlist { $setlist }, preset { $preset } ({ $name })
cli-set-param-about = Sets a parameter of a block in the active preset
cli-set-param-long = Changes one parameter of a block in the active preset. The change applies at once and is kept until another preset is selected; run `preset save` to store it.
cli-block-state-about = Switches a block of the active preset on or off
cli-block-state-long = Switches the block at the given path and position on or off. Like parameter changes, this is kept until another preset is selected unless the preset is saved.
cli-save-preset-about = Saves the active preset with its changes
cli-save-preset-long = Stores the active preset, including changed parameters and block states, in its own slot under its current name.
cli-path-help = Signal path, 1 or 2 (as in `preset blocks`: P1.3 is path 1).
cli-position-help = Position in the path, 1–8 (as in `preset blocks`: P1.3 is position 3).
cli-cab-help = Change a parameter of an amp+cab block's cab instead of its amp.
cli-param-help = Parameter name as `preset blocks` shows it (e.g. Drive, "Low Cut"), or its number.
cli-value-help = New value as `preset blocks` shows it (e.g. 4.5, 50%, 120ms, 8kHz, -3dB, on).
cli-state-help = Whether the block is on or off.
cli-block-not-found = Path { $path } has no block at position { $position }.
cli-params-unknown = The parameters of '{ $block }' are not known, so they cannot be changed.
cli-param-not-found = '{ $param }' is not a parameter of '{ $block }'.
cli-param-set = { $param } set to { $value }.
cli-block-state-set = Block P{ $path }.{ $position } switched { $state }.
cli-unsaved-hint = The change applies at once; run `preset save` to keep it.
cli-preset-saved = Saved "{ $name }" to setlist { $setlist }, preset { $preset }.
cli-set-model-about = Replaces the model of a block in the active preset
cli-set-model-long = Replaces the model of the block at the given path and position. The new model starts with its default parameters. A new amp keeps the cab of an amp+cab block unless --with-cab names another.
cli-add-block-about = Adds a block to the active preset
cli-add-block-long = Adds a block with the given model, switched on and with default parameters, at an empty path and position.
cli-remove-block-about = Removes a block from the active preset
cli-remove-block-long = Removes the block at the given path and position.
cli-model-help = Model name as `preset blocks` shows it (e.g. "Minotaur (mono)"; part of a name works if it is unique), or its ID.
cli-with-cab-help = Cab for an amp+cab block; --model then names the amp.
cli-model-not-found = No model matches '{ $model }'.
cli-model-ambiguous = '{ $model }' matches several models: { $candidates }.
cli-amp-cab-mismatch = An amp+cab block needs an amp as --model and a cab as --with-cab.
cli-position-taken = Path { $path }, position { $position } already holds '{ $block }'.
cli-model-set = P{ $path }.{ $position } is now { $model }.
cli-block-added = Added { $model } at P{ $path }.{ $position }.
cli-block-removed = Removed { $model } from P{ $path }.{ $position }.

mock-mode-active = [mock] Running in mock mode — no hardware required.

